WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:04.220
- Coffee's one of the most
consumed beverages in the world.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.692
Some people drink it daily.

00:00:05.692 --> 00:00:06.870
Some people drink it five times a day.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.810
Today, we're going to be talking

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.130
about all the effects
that it has on your body

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.425
that you would not expect.

00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:12.258
(indistinct)

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:14.150
I'm a little coffee-hyped.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.470
Most people associate
coffee with the sudden urge

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.340
to go to the bathroom.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.980
And that is true for some people.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.813
The reality is

00:00:19.813 --> 00:00:21.870
that coffee affects our
GI systems differently.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.070
And for some, it could
actually cause constipation

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.120
as opposed to diarrhea.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.370
And we're quick to blame
caffeine for the surge to go.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.220
But the reality is we
have research showing

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.220
that decaf coffee has similar effects,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.170
leading us to believe that
it's actually the result

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.760
of the secretion of the
hormone named gastrin,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.448
which actually promotes digestion.

00:00:37.448 --> 00:00:38.290
(slurping sound)

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.110
Coffee could absolutely
wreck your ability to sleep.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:41.943
Throughout the day,

00:00:41.943 --> 00:00:43.910
your body produces more
and more adenosine,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.560
which actually binds to receptors

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.460
generating a sleepy
response from your body.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.470
The longer that you're
awake, the more adenosine,

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.320
the more binding, the sleepier you are.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.700
Now coffee comes in with
its caffeine content

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.010
and starts blocking those
adenosine receptors,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.870
thereby making you feel less sleepy,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.870
thereby making it harder to fall asleep.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.980
So its intended effect can actually become

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.950
a negative effect.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.970
The caffeine can actually also
impact our circadian rhythm

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.380
through its effects on melatonin,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.950
which can confuse our internal clock.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.180
It's almost like having a form of jet lag

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.154
without any of the fun of travel.

00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:13.987
(slurping sound)

00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:14.820
I'll have a large coffee

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.650
with a double shot of anxiety, please.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.740
You can add all sorts of
tasty things to your coffee,

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.560
like cream, sugar, or any of this.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.940
Of course, unless you're drinking decaf,

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.120
your coffee is also loaded with caffeine.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.460
And while caffeine can be
useful in waking you up

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.610
and keeping you stimulated,

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.240
it can also cause a
jittery sensation nearby,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.800
causing you to be anxious or sweaty even.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.130
That's because it activates
the fight or flight response

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.690
in the body known as the
sympathetic nervous system.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.880
Research has even shown
that overdoing caffeine

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.660
by a small amount can
increase baseline anxiety

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.689
and the likelihood of panic attacks.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:45.522
(slurping sound)

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:47.710
Coffee can absolutely impact your weight,

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.200
as black coffee is nearly calorie-free

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.170
and actually kicks up your metabolic rate.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.420
And in fact, as caffeine
stimulates the production

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.290
of adrenaline, it also
decreases the level of ghrelin,

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.750
the hormone that makes you feel hungry

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:00.130
and your stomach growl.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.180
Grehlin, growl.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.740
But this effect holds true even for decaf,

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.710
because it has been shown
to increase the hormone

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:10.240
peptide YY, which actually
makes you feel satiated or full.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.490
And for intermittent
fasting fans like myself,

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.150
research has shown that
having a black cup of coffee

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.510
does not break your intermittent fast

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:18.950
and actually keeps the majority

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.910
of intermittent fasting benefits there.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.380
This means that black
coffee can truly be used

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.910
to aid in your weight loss efforts.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.350
Cheat code vibes.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:27.183
(slurping sound)

00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:28.470
Coffee makes your hands feel cold

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.500
because coffee stimulates
those small glands

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.700
that sit on top of your
kidneys called the adrenals.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.850
They secrete adrenaline

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.470
and a stress hormone known as cortisol.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.090
One of the main effects of adrenaline

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.280
is to constrict blood
vessels which are not

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.600
of utmost importance to your survival.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.780
That means all the small
blood vessels furthest away

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.080
from the midline of your
body, like in your fingertips

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.350
and your toes, they start
getting vasoconstricted.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.380
They start getting tighter,

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.870
which temporarily decreases
some of the circulation

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.550
to your hand, making them
feel cold and look pale.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:55.383
(slurping sound)

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.290
Caffeine is one of the most studied

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.120
performance enhancing drugs.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.652
PEDs? Yeah.

00:03:00.652 --> 00:03:01.485
Why?

00:03:01.485 --> 00:03:02.930
Because it works and has been shown

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.690
to have significant benefits

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.240
as long as you don't overuse it.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.160
Focus, endurance, strength, speed

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.610
have all been tested and
found to have been boosted

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.750
with low to moderate doses of caffeine

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.660
60 to 90 minutes before
workouts and competitions.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.180
That this effect is so great,

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:20.310
that the NCAA has actually
set a caffeine limit

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.143
for its athletes.

00:03:21.143 --> 00:03:23.480
They restrict the amount of
caffeine in an athlete's system

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.050
by limiting concentrations
to roughly 500 milligrams

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.265
of caffeine or several cups of coffee.

00:03:29.265 --> 00:03:30.150
(slurping sound)

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.570
It's no surprise that coffee
does raise the heart rate

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.420
and blood pressure temporarily due

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.470
to the secretion of
epinephrine, adrenaline.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.420
The interesting part is that
the effect has been found

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.290
to be true for decaf coffee as well.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.000
So another ingredient could
potentially be responsible here.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.370
It's also important to note
that long-term consumption

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.440
does not seem to cause hypertension.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.090
The thinking is that those who
consistently consume coffee

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.460
actually build up a
protective tolerance to it.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.710
Will say, though, that I
have treated individuals

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.700
who have gotten their blood
pressure under better control

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.370
by removing caffeine
from their diet entirely.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.228
Just saying.

00:04:00.228 --> 00:04:01.061
(slurping sound)

00:04:01.061 --> 00:04:02.740
Removing coffee's a double-edged sword

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.270
'cause it could cause withdrawal symptoms

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.370
as early as 12 to 24 hours.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.210
The thought behind caffeine
withdrawal headaches

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:09.690
is that the blood vessels in the brain,

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.700
which normally are kept
tight and constricted due

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.970
to the action of the caffeine,

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.850
start to swell and cause pain.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:15.990
The ironic part of this

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.010
is that caffeine is actually
found in some common

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.045
over-the-counter medications
like Excedrin Migraine.

00:04:21.045 --> 00:04:21.878
(slurping sound)

00:04:21.878 --> 00:04:23.650
Is coffee dehydrating?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.020
This one is fiercely
argued on online forums.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.510
Some say yes, some say no.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.440
Here's the truth.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.530
Coffee is a mild diuretic.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.520
It makes you pee more.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.970
It makes you excrete more fluids.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.310
However, if you're drinking
a full cup of coffee,

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.590
there's fluids in there,

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.790
so it replaces the fluids you lose, right?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.623
Yes.

00:04:40.623 --> 00:04:42.340
However, if you're
drinking little espressos

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.320
or espresso shots in your coffee,

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.210
and you're getting a ton
of caffeine in there,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:47.900
you're not replacing the loss fluid,

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.920
and then in that case, it
can be somewhat dehydrated.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.590
That being said, if
you're not overdoing it,

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:54.741
it's usually not enough
to become a problem.

00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:55.574
(slurping sound)

00:04:55.574 --> 00:04:58.120
My dear acid reflux sufferers,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.060
coffee can absolutely
impact your acid secretion.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:02.410
First of all, we need to stop

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.900
with this acid base obsession
that has developed online.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.580
Drinking electrolyte reduced water,

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.600
alkaline water is just complete nonsense.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.900
The reason coffee makes acid reflux worse

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.050
is much simpler than that.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.530
It is proven to stimulate gastrin release,

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.100
which increases gastric acid secretion.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.870
And this happens because of
the bitter taste of coffee

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.240
that activates a type two

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.170
bitter taste receptors in your mouth.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.510
So the bitter taste of coffee

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.468
makes your body secrete more acid.

00:05:27.468 --> 00:05:28.301
(explosion)

00:05:28.301 --> 00:05:29.134
(slurping sound)

00:05:29.134 --> 00:05:31.640
Coffee actually messes
with your medications

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.070
and it interacts with
them in one of three ways.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.770
First, it affects the absorption

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.020
of the medications and
studies have actually shown

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.150
that common over-the-counter
meds like ketoprofen,

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:43.220
which is very similar to
ibuprofen and paracetamol,

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.450
which is similar to Tylenol,

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:47.260
are significantly
impacted by coffee intake.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.760
The second is through the
disruption of the metabolism

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.380
of the medications through enzymes.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.060
For example, the blood
levels of clozapine, lithium,

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.630
warfarin, and several antidepressant drugs

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:59.570
actually were increased after
the ingestion of coffee,

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.880
making them more potent and
potentially increasing toxicity.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.690
And the third, is through
the disruption of excretion

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.523
of the drugs.

00:06:06.523 --> 00:06:07.790
Basically, how long they stick around.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.130
In fact, we've seen increased
excretion of minerals

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.350
like, calcium, magnesium,
sodium, chloride,

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.930
and even water-soluble
vitamins like vitamin B.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:15.763
Think about that.

00:06:15.763 --> 00:06:17.380
You're drinking coffee,
you're taking your meds,

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.680
and it's all going amuck.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.970
Coffee makes you pee.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.500
Here's the truth about holding your pee.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.340
Check this out now.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.420
It's a must-watch.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.000
As always, stay happy and
healthy, but watch this.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.430
There's a ton of great
comments and questions in here.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.263
Whoa.

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.686
(upbeat music)

